ailing health checks after v2.3.1 was deployed to production (us-east, us-west, eu-west); error rate was 0.18. Action taken: rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.3.1-rc was only in staging and was also unhealthy). Rollback status: us-east, us-west, and eu-west now report v2.3.0 with error rate 0.002. Next steps: confirm error rate stays low, investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any re-release.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 163530, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01P4C2SrvQoHunRc1piheQ5P", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 163530, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01P4C2SrvQoHunRc1piheQ5P", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 165888, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it is healthy again. Error rate dropped from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** v2.3.1 was the unhealthy release. v2.3.0 is the most recent production release marked healthy. v2.3.1-rc was only in staging and was also unhealthy. Because v2.3.0 has already been healthy in production, the change-manager approval policy did not apply. The rollback response also shows it was approved.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001** for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback, and the next steps, and it paged the on-call engineer. The first attempt timed out, so I checked that no incident had been created and then retried with the same idempotency key. Only one incident exists.\n- **Follow-up:** v2.3.1 needs investigation before it is released again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_011Q6QCVTFSBXU4VNPHDrfuQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01EQeYYecRQoD8es5pcS9hwP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is the unhealthy one currently running in all three regions. I'll roll back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012dixHLtrccatizvCSaXLwn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Q9ssPs5XipgE9vmS37wB3r", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01SeEQHojDyLXy1qfqFsL1jv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after v2.3.1 was deployed to production (us-east, us-west, eu-west); error rate was 0.18. Action taken: rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.3.1-rc was only in staging and was also unhealthy). Rollback status: us-east, us-west, and eu-west now report v2.3.0. Next steps: confirm error rate recovers, investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any re-release.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident"